# Copy to .env.local for local work. Every value is optional for `npm run dev`.
# Server-side only, unless a name starts with NEXT_PUBLIC_. None of these do, on purpose.
# Static pages read them at build time, so redeploy after changing one on the host.
# On Vercel they go in Settings, Environment Variables. On any other host, in its own environment settings
# (README, "Hosting somewhere other than Vercel").

# ---- Which copy of the site this is --------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel sets this on its own (VERCEL_ENV). On any other host, set SITE_ENV=production on the live site,
# or the Google tag and booking conversions stay off. Use SITE_ENV=preview on a test copy: it never emails
# Jimmy and never counts in Google Ads.
# SITE_ENV=production

# ---- Storage (bookings and firewood orders) ----------------------------------------------
# "supabase" for real data. Anything else means the in-memory demo store, which `npm run dev`
# allows automatically. A production server refuses it unless BOOKING_DEMO_MODE=true, and the
# real domain (ALLOW_INDEXING=true) refuses it always.
BOOKING_STORE=memory
# BOOKING_DEMO_MODE=true
# BOOKING_DEMO_SEED=off

# Needed when BOOKING_STORE=supabase. Never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# The key is the server key from Supabase, Settings, API Keys: either the newer secret key (sb_secret_...)
# or the older service_role key (eyJ...). Never the publishable or anon key.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---- Seasonal mode -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firewood is switched off in content/season.ts right now, which overrides both of these.
# gutter (default): "/" is the gutter site. firewood: "/" is firewood, gutters move to /gutters.
# SITE_MODE=gutter
# Shows /firewood and the mode switch without changing "/". Vercel previews do this on their own.
# FIREWOOD_PREVIEW=true

# ---- Stripe (firewood checkout) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Test keys only until launch: sk_test_... from the Stripe dashboard.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_
# From `stripe listen` locally, or the webhook endpoint's page in the dashboard.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_
# Leave unset. Real payments need this AND a live key AND Supabase AND every item in
# content/firewood.ts marked "confirmed". See the launch checklist in the README.
# STRIPE_ALLOW_LIVE_PAYMENTS=true

# ---- Notifications to Jimmy (FormSubmit) ---------------------------------------------------
# Emails every booking and plan request to the email in content/site.ts. No key needed.
# Production only. Until Jimmy activates FormSubmit, each submission sends him an activation email,
# so read README "Activating and testing" before turning this on. Ignored on previews and the demo store.
# FORMSUBMIT_ENABLED=true
# /notify-test sends Jimmy one test email. Off (a 404) unless this is "true". Turn it on only while testing.
# NOTIFY_TEST_ENABLED=true
# Signs the "Check it's real" links in Jimmy's emails. Optional: without it the server uses a secret derived
# from SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Changing either one stops the links in older emails from working.
# NOTICE_SECRET=

# ---- Daily keep-alive (vercel.json "crons" on Vercel, .github/workflows/keepalive.yml elsewhere) ----
# Optional. If set, /api/keepalive only answers callers that send it as a Bearer token: Vercel's scheduler
# does that on its own; off Vercel, put the same value in GitHub as the CRON_SECRET secret.
# CRON_SECRET=

# ---- Firewood order emails (Resend, server-side; dormant) ---------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=Keystone Gutter Glow <bookings@keystonegutterglow.com>

# ---- Site --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public URL for canonical/OG/schema links, the links in Jimmy's emails and Stripe's return page.
# On Vercel it defaults to Vercel's domain. On any other host, set it to wherever the site lives:
# unset there, links point at keystonegutterglow.com.
# SITE_URL=https://keystonegutterglow.com
# Set to "true" only on the real domain, so previews and the mockup never get indexed.
# ALLOW_INDEXING=true
